Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

Practice Overview &nbsp;

WPP Media Data, Tech &amp; Analytics is WPP’s data, analytics, and technology services division. We’re on a mission to transform marketing by leveraging the fastest, most connected data platform that bridges marketing strategy to scaled activation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Our team works with agencies and clients to transform the value of data by bringing together technology, data and analytics capabilities. We deliver this through analytically minded people leveraging AI and tech to drive real business change for our clients. We’re endlessly curious. Our team of analytical thinkers, builders, creators and problem solvers are over 1,000 strong, across 20 markets around the world. Within our UK Data, Tech and Analytics team we host three core practices - Modelling Services, Applied Analytics and Data Science and Solutions.&nbsp;

The Data Science &amp; Solutions practice is the innovation engine and technical accelerator for WPP Media Data, Tech &amp; Analytics Division in the UK. We bridge advanced data science, artificial intelligence, and software engineering to solve high-value client challenges and supercharge agency capabilities. The practice operates at the intersection of technical innovation and commercial media application-incubating proprietary analytical tools, advancing AI adoption, and delivering specialised machine learning models that go beyond traditional econometrics. We strive to be the benchmark for intelligent, ethical and commercially transformative decisioning through applied data science.

Team Summary and Remit &nbsp;

Sitting alongside Modelling Services and Applied Analytics within our 120-strong UK Analytics organisation, the Data Science &amp; Solutions team has two core mandates:&nbsp;

• Advanced Tool &amp; Solution Development: Designing, engineering, and productising bespoke analytical applications, automation pipelines, and AI-enabled tools that elevate the speed, sophistication, and efficiency of our wider Modelling and Applied Analytics teams.&nbsp;

• Specialised Modelling &amp; Advanced Analytics (Role Focus): Delivering high-impact data science assignments requiring techniques beyond the core scope of Marketing Mix Modelling (MMM), such as customer lifetime value (CLV), propensity and churn modelling, advanced incrementality algorithms, and price elasticity. &nbsp;

This Director role will focus on the second of the two above - Specialised Modelling and Advanced Analytics, helping to enhance the implementation of our&nbsp;internal solutions related to this. Our other director's remit sits in the first area of mandates. There is of course collaboration - but we are looking for someone to bring expertise in the second mandate of the team.&nbsp;

These mandates&nbsp;are delivered in line with our principles - Value, Scale and Innovation . Turning complex data signals into undeniable business growth for our clients. Being trusted co-pilots who make solutions scalable, interpretable and actionable. Working in a high trust, high impact environment where innovation yields measurable consequence.&nbsp;

